---
id: RS-008
type: rule
family: rust-reliability
title: clone() inside syntactic loop
version: 1

severity: info
confidence: medium
spectrum_position: 8

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.rs]
allowlist: []

detection:
  type: ast
  ast_query: '(call_expression function: (field_expression field: (field_identifier) @method)) @target'

related: []
enabled: true
opt_in: true
---

A `.clone()` inside a `for`, `while`, or `loop` body may allocate repeatedly or
hide avoidable ownership churn. Hoist invariant clones, borrow when lifetime-safe,
or use deliberate shared ownership such as `Arc::clone` where that is the real
intent. If the clone is cheap or required for ownership transfer, suppress with
that reason.

This rule is **opt-in** and syntactic. It does not attempt a type-cost model, and
it deliberately does not cover iterator-adapter closures or UFCS
`Clone::clone(...)` calls in this first wave.
